The Shrewd Dude wrote:
>>From the pratical, to the hilarious, share your experiences with us,
> for newer players to get on their feet, or older players to fall off
> them laughing.

  *  If monsters suddenly seem a lot tougher, check the ( and ] commands.

  *  When disposing of junk in the minetown temple, walk into the corner 
and *drop* it.  Do *not* throw it into the corner ("The dart slips as 
you throw it!  The priestess get angry!").

  *  If the minetown watch (or other tough peacefuls) are around, do not 
kick stuff.

  *  Learn what the [)*"=( commands do, and be sure to use them, 
especially when cockatrices are around.

  *  A cockatrice corpse is probably the most dangerous thing in the game.

  *  Do not use the key ) or / when putting stuff in a BoH.

  *  Use control, shift, g, or G instead of holding down direction keys, 
as TGWTWOD may come by at the most inconvenient moment.

  *  Black dragons can move and blast you in the same turn.  Do not play 
with them.

  *  Do not attempt to edit with the arrow keys.

  *  Get into the habit of resting for a few turns after eating. This 
will avoid accidentally attacking things if you get confused, especially 
priests.

  *  Move very cautiously in Sokoban.  On the top level, give due 
consideration to the F command when you encounter the mimics.

  *  Take careful note of when your spells are running out.  #name-ing 
the spellbooks types with the current turn immediately after reading 
them is handy.

  *  Never put food in the 'y' slot.

